{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"3332","artifact_type":"code-review","name":"code-review-T1-qg-docs-backlog-item-groomed-schema-field-drift@sha256:26bdae5462adcca3e8ab6b8e29d33dc50e9c30efcd67c1787910fa5f395e2ea0"},"owner_reference":"3332","content":"# Code Review: T1 \u2014 Code Review\n\n**Verdict:** FAIL\n**Reviewer:** code-reviewer (independent, SAM Stage 6, quality-gate plan Paf145f48)\n**Reviewed implementation:** #3332, implementation plan P74e3c201 (T1 apply-edits, T2 goal-backward verify \u2014 both marked `complete`)\n**Stack:** Documentation (Markdown, prose) \u2014 no code, no interfaces\n**Stack Skills Loaded:** none applicable (`dh:code-review-*` stack table has no entry for a plain `docs/*.md` prose file with no frontmatter/skill-agent structure; universal rules applied only, per code-reviewer SOP fallback)\n\n---\n\n## Acceptance Criteria Status\n\nNine criteria, from `backlog_view(selector=\"#3332\", sections=[\"Acceptance Criteria\"])`, verified independently against the committed file (`plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md` at HEAD `8752b23a4`) and primary sources (`backlog_core/models.py`, `plugins/development-harness/AGENTS.md`, `research/README.md`) \u2014 not against T1/T2's self-reports.\n\n| # | Criterion | Status | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Frontmatter no longer shows `name:` as a schema field | MET | `grep -n 'name' <doc>` \u2192 only hit is `:58` \"function names\" (incidental prose, out of scope). Line 15 = `title: \"Item title\"`. |\n| 2 | Frontmatter matches `BacklogItem` real fields (`models.py:1011-1013`) | MET | `models.py:1011-1013` = `title: str`, `reference: str`, `description: str`. Doc has `title` + `description` at top level, `metadata:` block below; `reference` correctly omitted (internally-managed field, not author-set \u2014 architect spec Edit 1 note). |\n| 3 | Storage section drops the single hardcoded per-item path | MET | Line 5 (`**Scope**:`) contains no `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/backlog/{priority}-{slug}.md` / `dh_paths.backlog_dir()` reference. `grep -n 'backlog/{priority}\\|\\.dh/projects\\|dh_paths.backlog_dir' <doc>` \u2192 zero hits. |\n| 4 | Storage description holds for all four backends (github/sqlite/memory/beads) | MET | Line 5 names all four backends explicitly, states format/location are backend internals, cites `plugins/development-harness/AGENTS.md` \u00a7Backend Providers with the plugin-scoped path (unambiguous from the doc's location) \u2014 section confirmed present at `AGENTS.md:537-544`. |\n| 5 | Status vocabulary == `_VALID_STATUSES` (`models.py:723`) | MET | `models.py:723` = `{\"open\",\"done\",\"in-progress\",\"needs-grooming\",\"closed\"}` (verified by direct grep+read in this review, not trusted from the architect spec). Doc line 23 matches member-for-member; `resolved` removed. |\n| 6 | **No other file changes are introduced** | **UNMET** | `git show --stat 8752b23a4` (the landed fix commit) touches **4 files**, not 1: the target doc plus `plugins/development-harness/.claude-plugin/plugin.json`, `.codex-plugin/plugin.json`, `.cursor-plugin/plugin.json` (each a version bump). This is a hard, unconditional AC in the item body (\"this item's scope is limited to `docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md`\"), and is not satisfied by the actual commit. |\n| 7 | `~:46` prose rule references `title`, not `name` | MET | Doc line 46: \"Do **not** duplicate `title`, `description`, `source`, `added`, `priority`, `type`, `issue`\u2026\". Same zero-match grep as #1 confirms no residual `name`. |\n| 8 | Priority vocabulary == `_VALID_PRIORITIES` (`models.py:721`), with the required `completed` annotation | MET | `models.py:721` = `{\"P0\",\"P1\",\"P2\",\"Ideas\",\"completed\"}` \u2014 verified directly. Doc line 21 = `P0\\|P1\\|P2\\|Ideas\\|completed  # \"completed\" is set internally on completion, not chosen by the groomer` \u2014 matches the plan's mandated annotation text exactly. |\n| 9 | `~:11` relative link resolves to the real `research/README.md` | MET | Doc line 11 = `../../../research/README.md`. `plugins/development-harness/docs/` \u2192 3 `../` hops reaches repo root. `test -f research/README.md` at repo root \u2192 `ROOT_OK`; the resolved relative path (`plugins/development-harness/docs/../../../research/README.md`) points at the same real file. |\n\n**8 of 9 criteria MET. AC #6 UNMET.**\n\n---\n\n## Root cause of the AC #6 gap (independently confirmed, not merely restated from T2)\n\n`plugins/development-harness/.pre-commit-config.yaml:160-166` registers `auto-sync-manifests`\n(`files: ^plugins/`, `pass_filenames: false`) \u2014 it runs, unconditionally, on *any* commit that\ntouches a file under `plugins/`, and rewrites the three plugin manifest version fields. This is\nnot something the implementing task authored or could have avoided without bypassing a\nrepository-mandated pre-commit hook (itself prohibited absent explicit user instruction).\n\nThis is not implementer error: the same three-file manifest-bump pattern appears on the two\ncommits immediately preceding this one in the repo's own history \u2014\n`git show --stat e0fb48d1e` and `git show --stat 1dbbd8208` both show identical\n`.claude-plugin/plugin.json` / `.codex-plugin/plugin.json` / `.cursor-plugin/plugin.json`\nversion-only diffs alongside unrelated substantive changes. A single-file commit touching\n`plugins/development-harness/docs/*.md` is structurally impossible under the repo's current\nhook configuration.\n\nThis finding is not new \u2014 T2 (`dh:feature-verifier`, implementation plan P74e3c201) already\nsurfaced it as a GAP with the same evidence and the same root-cause attribution. This review\nindependently re-derived it from primary sources (pre-commit config + git history) rather than\ntrusting T2's report, and it reproduces identically.\n\n---\n\n## Universal Findings\n\nPure prose/documentation change \u2014 most universal dimensions (security, tests, API contracts,\nerror handling, performance) are not applicable. Findings limited to what applies:\n\n### Blocking (Required Changes)\n\n- **[CONTRACT]** `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md` (commit `8752b23a4`) \u2014 AC #6 (\"No other file changes are introduced\") is unmet: the landed commit modifies 3 plugin manifest files in addition to the target doc. This is the sole blocking finding. **Required change is not a rework of the six text edits** (all independently verified correct above) \u2014 it is a decision on AC #6 itself: either (a) amend the item's AC #6 wording to explicitly except pre-commit-hook-generated manifest version bumps (recommended \u2014 matches T2's suggested remedy and the repo's own established norm for `plugins/`-scoped commits), or (b) if the literal single-file constraint is truly load-bearing, split the manifest bumps into a separate commit and confirm whether the hook can be satisfied that way (unverified whether `auto-sync-manifests` can run pre-commit and still land as a second commit \u2014 this review did not test that path, as it edits nothing).\n\n### Non-Blocking (Recommendations)\n\n- None. The six textual corrections match the architect spec's before/after text verbatim, are internally consistent (both `name`\u2192`title` occurrences fixed together per Edit 1/4), and are corroborated against primary sources (`models.py`, `AGENTS.md`, `research/README.md`) rather than the spec's quotations of them.\n\n---\n\n## Stack-Specific Findings\n\nNo stack skill applied (plain documentation, no frontmatter/skill/agent structure matching the `dh:code-review-*` detection table). None.\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\n**Files reviewed:** 1 target file (`plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md`) + 3 incidentally-touched manifest files + primary sources (`backlog_core/models.py`, `plugins/development-harness/AGENTS.md`, `research/README.md`, `.pre-commit-config.yaml`)\n**Acceptance criteria:** 8/9 MET\n**Blocking findings:** 1 (AC #6 scope gate)\n**Non-blocking findings:** 0\n\nAll six specified text corrections are textually and semantically correct, verified independently\nagainst `backlog_core/models.py`'s live vocabulary constants and `BacklogItem`'s real field set,\nagainst `plugins/development-harness/AGENTS.md`'s Backend Providers section, and against the\nexistence and correct relative depth of `research/README.md`. Nothing in the doc content itself\nwarrants rework. The single blocking finding \u2014 AC #6's single-file scope gate \u2014 is real and\nindependently reproduced from the commit history and the repository's own pre-commit\nconfiguration, but it is caused by a repo-wide, pre-existing, unconditional pre-commit hook that\nbumps three plugin manifests on every commit touching `plugins/`, not by any implementation\nchoice in this task. This is the identical gap T2 already reported (GAPS_FOUND) under the\nimplementation plan; this independent quality-gate review reproduces it from primary sources and\nconfirms it is still present in the merged state. Verdict is FAIL on the strict letter of AC #6;\nthe recommended remedy is an orchestrator/backlog-owner decision to amend AC #6's wording (accept\nhook-generated manifest bumps as out of the literal scope gate) rather than any further edit to\nthe reviewed file.\n"}